cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PyroWISE — wildfire-spread simulation engine"
message: "If you use PyroWISE or build on its open scientific documentation, please cite it as follows."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Infordata Sistemi Srl Società Benefit"
    city: "Trieste"
    country: "IT"
    website: "https://infordata.it"
repository-code: "https://github.com/infordata-sistemi/pyrowise"
url: "https://github.com/infordata-sistemi/pyrowise"
abstract: >
  PyroWISE is a wildfire-spread simulation engine combining the Rothermel
  surface-fire-spread model (Rothermel, 1972) with Huygens-wavefront
  perimeter propagation (Anderson et al., 1982; Finney, 1998), calibrated
  for the cross-border Karst region of Italy and Slovenia. It is the
  simulation core of the TerraWise territorial-emergency platform and the
  Karst Firewall 5.0 EU Interreg project (ITA-SI0600146, 2024–2027).
keywords:
  - wildfire
  - fire-spread simulation
  - Rothermel
  - Huygens propagation
  - digital twin
  - Karst
  - Interreg
  - TerraWise
